# Bilby environment.
#
# Copy to web/.env.local for development, or paste each value into the Vercel
# project settings for production. Never commit a filled in copy of this file:
# .gitignore blocks .env and .env.local, and that guard is the only thing
# between a secret and a public history.
#
# With NONE of these set the app still runs against a mock supplier, which is
# deliberate: a fresh clone must start without an account anywhere. DATABASE_URL
# is the one exception, because there is no local file fallback any more.

# ── Hostnames ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only set these to move off the defaults. Every other hostname derives from
# APEX, so this is the one string that relocates the whole customer surface.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APEX=bilbymobile.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CORP_APEX=nextwave.au

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres, on Supabase. Required: there is no local file fallback any more.
#
# Use the TRANSACTION POOLER string, port 6543, from Supabase under
# Settings, Database, Connection string. Not the direct connection on 5432:
# a serverless deployment opens far more connections than that will accept,
# and the failure looks like the database being down.
#
#   postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
DATABASE_URL=

# ── Sessions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two DIFFERENT random values, 32 bytes each. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# They must not match. A shared key would let a customer session be replayed
# against the staff console, which is the exact thing the separate admin domain
# exists to prevent.
SESSION_SECRET=
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# The first staff account. Anyone who can read this address can request a sign
# in link, so it should be a mailbox only you control.
OWNER_EMAIL=

# ── Suppliers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absent credentials mean that provider stays disabled in the registry rather
# than throwing. Enable each one from the staff console once its key is set.
ESIMACCESS_API_KEY=
AIRALO_CLIENT_ID=
AIRALO_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Which vendor the eSIM fulfiller calls. "mock" until a real account is funded.
PAID_SUPPLIER=mock

# ── Payments ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With no secret key the shop still renders and the buy button says so plainly.
# Nothing can be charged.
#
# The webhook secret is NOT optional once the secret key is set. An endpoint
# that skips signature verification is an endpoint where anybody who finds the
# URL can mint paid orders, so an unset secret makes the handler refuse every
# event rather than trust one.
#
# Get it from the Stripe dashboard under Developers, Webhooks, after adding an
# endpoint pointing at:
#   https://app.<your apex>/api/webhooks/stripe
#
# Subscribe it to at least:
#   checkout.session.completed
#   checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded
#   checkout.session.async_payment_failed
#   checkout.session.expired
#   charge.dispute.created
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Not used. Checkout is hosted by Stripe on their own domain, so no key is
# needed in the browser and no card field exists in this application. Kept as a
# note rather than a variable so nobody adds Elements without reading why.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ── Email ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No key means no receipts, no eSIM delivery and no account recovery. Account
# recovery is the only route back in for a customer, because there are no
# passwords.
RESEND_API_KEY=
MAIL_FROM=hello@bilbymobile.com

# ── Analytics, all default OFF ──────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_CONVERSION_LABEL=

# ── Observability ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SENTRY_DSN=

# ── Legal ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not printed on any page. Kept here because invoices and the Play Console
# still require it.
LEGAL_ABN=
